# The Depot on native - environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every .env file in this repo is gitignored;
# this template is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local

# Where apps/express-api is reachable from the device running this app.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is not decoration: Expo inlines these into the app bundle at build
# time, so anything here is readable by anyone who has the app - exactly as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is readable by anyone with the page. An API URL is fine to
# publish. A secret key never is, and the reason this app needs none is that the
# Express server holds it and this only ever talks to /billing.
#
# localhost is a trap. It works in the iOS simulator and on web, and nowhere
# else:
#
#   iOS simulator      http://localhost:4000
#   Android emulator   http://10.0.2.2:4000     (the host, as the emulator sees it)
#   physical device    http://192.168.x.x:4000  (your machine's LAN IP)
#
# A wrong value here fails as a bare "network request failed" with nothing
# pointing at the cause, so the shop floor prints the address it tried.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
